# Pirate English, an example translation of the Special K Injection Frontend (SKIF).
#
# Arr! This be a complete translation into the tongue o' the seven seas, meant as an example
#   fer translators: it shows a finished .po file, with every placeholder, [link], line break
#     and plural form kept as the README (resources\l10n\README.md) asks. It is not embedded
#       in SKIF.exe. To try it, copy it to <Special K folder>\Languages\, restart SKIF, and pick
#         "Pirate English" in Settings > Appearance > Language.
#
# "en@pirate" (as Poedit writes it; SKIF reads it as the private-use tag en-x-pirate) is a language
#   Windows has no name for, so the X-Language-Name header gives the name shown in the language
#     picker. Real translations use a regular language (e.g. de, pt_BR) and do not need that header.
#       SKIF never picks this language on its own: it has to be chosen in the settings.
#
